Here's a Quick Start to get you interacting with the `fdic-gov` API:

```typescript
// Example: Retrieving an image asset.
// Assumes the asset ID "example_image.png" is known.
async function getImageAsset() {
  try {
    const assetData = await client.get_WRSiteInterceptEngine_Asset_php({ asset: "example_image.png" });
    // Process the image data (e.g., save to file, display in UI).
    console.log("Asset retrieved:", assetData);
    return assetData;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error retrieving asset:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
// Example: Submitting targeting data.
// This sends some sample targeting information to the FDIC website.
async function submitTargetingData() {
  const targetingParams = {
    page_url: "https://www.fdic.gov/example",
    user_agent: "Mozilla/5.0",
    screen_resolution: "1920x1080"
  };

  try {
    const response = await client.post_WRSiteInterceptEngine_Targeting_php(targetingParams);
    console.log("Targeting data submitted:", response);
    return response;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error submitting targeting data:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

